sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as REST Client
    participant Proxy as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant API as eval-hub API<br/>8080/TCP HTTP/HTTPS
    participant DB as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP SQL
    participant K8s as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Init as eval-runtime-init<br/>Init Container
    participant S3 as S3 / Git / HuggingFace<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Adapter as Provider Adapter<br/>lm-eval / RAGAS / Garak
    participant Sidecar as eval-runtime-sidecar<br/>Reverse Proxy
    participant Model as Model Endpoint<br/>HTTPS
    participant MLflow as MLflow Server<br/>HTTPS

    Note over Client,MLflow: Flow 1: Evaluation Job Lifecycle

    Client->>Proxy: POST /api/v1/evaluations/jobs<br/>Auth: Bearer Token
    Proxy->>API: Forward request<br/>X-User, X-Tenant headers
    API->>DB: Store evaluation record<br/>Tenant-scoped insert
    DB-->>API: OK
    API->>K8s: Create Job + ConfigMap<br/>+ Secret + NetworkPolicy<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount
    K8s-->>API: Job created
    API-->>Proxy: 201 Created
    Proxy-->>Client: Evaluation job response

    Note over Init,S3: Init Container Phase
    K8s->>Init: Start init container<br/>Mount secrets
    Init->>S3: Download test data<br/>Auth: AWS creds / Token
    S3-->>Init: Test data artifacts
    Note over Init: Exit after download

    Note over Adapter,MLflow: Evaluation Phase
    Adapter->>Sidecar: Inference request<br/>HTTP (pod-local, no TLS)
    Sidecar->>Model: Forward with SA token injection<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    Model-->>Sidecar: Inference response
    Sidecar-->>Adapter: Proxied response

    Adapter->>Sidecar: Log results to MLflow
    Sidecar->>MLflow: Forward with SA token<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    MLflow-->>Sidecar: OK
    Sidecar-->>Adapter: OK

    Adapter->>Sidecar: Callback: job complete
    Sidecar->>Proxy: POST events<br/>SA token
    Proxy->>API: Forward callback<br/>X-User, X-Tenant
    API->>DB: Update job status
    DB-->>API: OK

    Note over Client,MLflow: Flow 2: MCP Agent Interaction

    participant MCP as evalhub-mcp<br/>3001/TCP

    Client->>Proxy: MCP request<br/>Auth: Bearer Token
    Proxy->>MCP: Forward<br/>X-User, X-Tenant
    MCP->>API: REST API call<br/>Auth: Bearer Token
    API-->>MCP: Response
    MCP-->>Proxy: MCP response
    Proxy-->>Client: Response

    Note over Client,MLflow: Flow 3: Metrics Scrape

    participant Prom as Prometheus

    Prom->>API: GET /metrics<br/>Port 8081/TCP HTTP<br/>No auth
    API-->>Prom: Prometheus metrics
